{
  "reports": [
    {
      "title": "Synthetic Grid Station A: Cooling Control Failure and Transformer Overheat",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "The controller's software contained a start setpoint of 85°C instead of 75°C for the forced cooling groups.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The primary pump motor overload relay was set to trip at 38 A, lower than the motor's rated 40 A.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The backup fan's blade angle was fixed at zero after a field reassembly in April.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The temperature alarm transmitter remained off-line following a scheduled test earlier in the week.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "On 2026-09-08, the ambient air temperature reached 45°C and stayed there for eight hours.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The grid dispatcher raised the transformer export loading to 108% of nameplate.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The controller commanded pump startup when the transformer's oil temperature hit 85°C.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0, 4, 5]
        },
        {
          "text": "The primary pump motor tripped on its overload relay within 0.1 seconds after starting.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [1, 6]
        },
        {
          "text": "In automatic sequence, the controller started the backup fan, whose zero-pitch blades produced negligible airflow.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [2, 7]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer's top oil temperature climbed from 85°C to 96°C during the next twenty minutes.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [7, 8]
        },
        {
          "text": "An overheat alarm came into being at 96°C, but its network path was blocked by the disabled transmitter.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [3, 9]
        },
        {
          "text": "Generated gas within the transformer actuated the Buchholz relay and issued a protective trip command.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer isolated from the grid at 15:27, leaving the synthetic polymer plant without power.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "After the event, laboratory analysis ruled out any overvoltage; thermal aging alone had cracked the bushings.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The winding displacement test after trip exposed plastic deformation in the low-voltage winding.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The combined repair and outage losses reached an estimated $1.8 million for the synthetic utility.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12, 13]
        },
        {
          "text": "A calibration service corrected the controller's temperature setpoint to the design value of 75°C.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The motor overload relay was replaced and set with a trip current of 40 A.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [1]
        },
        {
          "text": "The backup fan was re-pitched and its performance test at full load confirmed rated airflow.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [2]
        },
        {
          "text": "The temperature alarm transmitter was powered back on and added to the standard functional test list.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [3]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Synthetic Transformer Bank T-4: Loss of Cooling Due to PLC Restart and Sensor Biases",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "The PLC watchdog timer had a 10 ms timeout, but its actual program scan period was 18 ms.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Contaminants on the temperature sensing element created a constant negative offset of 7°C.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The contactor coil's minimum pick-up voltage was higher than the station's 85% control voltage.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Dust and debris had jammed the emergency air intake louver in the completely closed position.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "On September 8, the ambient temperature remained above 42°C for 10 hours, adding heat input.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A system instruction ordered transformer loading to 115% for the afternoon peak.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 14:32, a self-test extended the PLC scan to 19.5 ms; the 10 ms watchdog then forced a restart.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The main cooling pump's contactor stayed open after the restart, its coil seeing only 85% of rated voltage.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [2, 6]
        },
        {
          "text": "Transformer oil, already heated by the 115% load and 45°C ambient, reached a top temperature of 96°C.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [4, 5, 7]
        },
        {
          "text": "With the sensor offset, the controller read 89°C while the true top oil temperature was 96°C.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [1, 8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The emergency fan started but delivered no forced air because the intake louver was jammed shut.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [3, 7]
        },
        {
          "text": "The controller's temperature input stayed under 92°C, leaving the high-temperature alarm unasserted.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9, 10]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer's internal pressure opened the spring relief valve at 15:20, disconnecting the unit.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The post-trip inspection found no shorted turns in the windings; heat had softened the insulating paper.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The trip left a 40 MW deficit; automatic under-frequency load shedding removed 25 MW of industrial load.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer replacement and rental transformer cost $3.5 million for a twelve-day outage.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12, 13]
        },
        {
          "text": "Adjusted the PLC watchdog to 25 ms and disabled automatic self-test during loaded operation.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "Cleaned and recalibrated the temperature sensor, effectively removing the constant 7°C offset.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [1]
        },
        {
          "text": "Installed a contactor with a lower pick-up voltage and added a dedicated control power regulator.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [2]
        },
        {
          "text": "Repaired the louver drive and added a proximity switch to show its open or closed state.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [3]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
